# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, you will learn how to classically simulate `QuantumCircuit` instances to estimate expectation values entirely through the means of OBP.\n"
msgstr "Dalam panduan ini, anda akan mempelajari cara mensimulasikan contoh `QuantumCircuit` secara klasik untuk menganggar nilai jangkaan sepenuhnya melalui OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since OBP will take an observable and backpropagate it through a given circuit, the \"simulation\" of a circuit amounts to computing the expectation value of the target observable with respect to this circuit.\n"
"As you will see later, the `qiskit-addon-obp` package is even capable of handling simple noise models, allowing you to compute noisy expectation values, too!\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan OBP akan mengambil observable dan merambat baliknya melalui litar tertentu, \"simulasi\" sesuatu litar bermaksud mengira nilai jangkaan observable sasaran berkenaan litar ini.\n"
"Seperti yang akan anda lihat nanti, pakej `qiskit-addon-obp` malah mampu mengendalikan model hingar yang ringkas, membolehkan anda mengira nilai jangkaan berhingar juga!\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Constructing an example circuit {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"
msgstr "Membina litar contoh {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the purposes of this guide, we will use the same example circuit as in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"
msgstr "Bagi tujuan panduan ini, kami akan menggunakan litar contoh yang sama seperti dalam [panduan pemangkasan sebutan Pauli](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the above is purely the circuit describing the time evolution under a chosen Hamiltonian.\n"
"We also need an initial state to start from, with respect to which we compute the expectation values of our observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, litar di atas semata-mata menerangkan evolusi masa di bawah Hamiltonian yang dipilih.\n"
"Kita juga memerlukan keadaan awal sebagai permulaan, yang berkenaannya kita mengira nilai jangkaan observable kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we could choose the all-zero (or vacuum) state as our initial state, but to show how one would insert their own initial state, we choose a different one below.\n"
msgstr "Sudah tentu, kita boleh memilih keadaan semua-sifar (atau vakum) sebagai keadaan awal kita, tetapi untuk menunjukkan cara memasukkan keadaan awal sendiri, kita memilih yang berbeza di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One possibility, would be to prepend the initial state to our time-evolution circuit above: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"But since we have already sliced our `circuit`, it is easier to simply insert the initial state as the first slice, which we do below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu kemungkinan ialah menambah keadaan awal di hadapan litar evolusi masa kita di atas: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"Tetapi memandangkan kita telah pun menghiris `circuit` kita, lebih mudah untuk sekadar memasukkan keadaan awal sebagai hirisan pertama, yang kita lakukan di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this way, we can simply replace the first slice with another initial state, if we want to exchange that in the future, without having to recompute our slices.\n"
msgstr "Dengan cara ini, kita boleh menggantikan hirisan pertama dengan keadaan awal lain, jika kita mahu menukarnya pada masa hadapan, tanpa perlu mengira semula hirisan kita.\n"

