msgstr "Sebagai semakan kewarasan (dan untuk membuktikan bahawa ini berfungsi) kita boleh membandingkan keputusan kita dengan `Statevector` Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some notes on performance {#some-notes-on-performance}"
msgstr "Beberapa catatan tentang prestasi {#some-notes-on-performance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The computational efficiency of the `backpropagate` call above will heavily depend on many things, including:\n"
"- the structure of the `circuit`\n"
"- the method of slicing the circuit\n"
"- the target observable\n"
"- the truncation parameters\n"
msgstr ""
"Kecekapan pengiraan panggilan `backpropagate` di atas akan sangat bergantung pada banyak perkara, termasuk:\n"
"- struktur `circuit`\n"
"- kaedah menghiris litar\n"
"- observable sasaran\n"
"- parameter pemangkasan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the `backpropagate` method simplifies the observable after every _slice_ has been applied, the number of gates in a slice can dramatically influence the computational burden.\n"
"The most aggressive strategy in terms of operator simplification can be achieved by slicing your circuit into slices of individual gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan kaedah `backpropagate` memudahkan observable selepas setiap _hirisan_ diterapkan, bilangan gate dalam sesuatu hirisan boleh mempengaruhi beban pengiraan dengan ketara.\n"
"Strategi paling agresif dari segi pemudahan operator boleh dicapai dengan menghiris litar anda kepada hirisan gate individu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can leverage all of the truncation mechanism built into the `backpropagate` method.\n"
"We did not do so above, effectively resulting in an exact expectation value, but you can learn how to in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, anda boleh memanfaatkan semua mekanisme pemangkasan yang terbina dalam kaedah `backpropagate`.\n"
"Kami tidak berbuat demikian di atas, sehingga menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang tepat, tetapi anda boleh mempelajari caranya dalam [panduan pemangkasan sebutan Pauli](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating a noisy expectation value {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Mensimulasikan nilai jangkaan berhingar {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit-addon-obp` package also supports handling of noise models in the form of `PauliLindbladError`s.\n"
"This is especially useful when you have characterized the noise model of the 2-qubit layers in your circuit, for example using the [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pakej `qiskit-addon-obp` turut menyokong pengendalian model hingar dalam bentuk `PauliLindbladError`.\n"
"Ini amat berguna apabila anda telah mencirikan model hingar lapisan 2 qubit dalam litar anda, contohnya menggunakan [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, you will see how you can use the `LayerError` objects returned by the `NoiseLearner` to compute noisy expectation values using OBP.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian ini, anda akan melihat cara menggunakan objek `LayerError` yang dikembalikan oleh `NoiseLearner` untuk mengira nilai jangkaan berhingar menggunakan OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obtaining a noise model {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"
msgstr "Mendapatkan model hingar {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, you would execute the `NoiseLearner` to obtain a noise model of your specific circuit.\n"
"To avoid complexity (and randomness) in this tutorial, we will refrain from doing so, and instead hard-code some noise model for our circuit below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lazimnya, anda akan melaksanakan `NoiseLearner` untuk mendapatkan model hingar bagi litar khusus anda.\n"
"Untuk mengelakkan kerumitan (dan kerawakan) dalam tutorial ini, kami tidak akan berbuat demikian, sebaliknya mengekodkan secara tetap beberapa model hingar untuk litar kita di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, we make sure that the structure of our data matches that of the [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"In its current (non-transpiled) form, our circuit contains 4 unique layers of 2-qubit gates:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[2]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[3]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[4]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, kami memastikan struktur data kita sepadan dengan [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"Dalam bentuknya sekarang (tidak ditranspil), litar kita mengandungi 4 lapisan unik gate 2 qubit:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: yang mempunyai gate `Rxx` bertindak pada semua pasangan qubit ganjil\n"
"- `slices[2]`: yang mempunyai gate `Rxx` bertindak pada semua pasangan qubit genap\n"
"- `slices[3]`: yang mempunyai gate `Ryy` bertindak pada semua pasangan qubit ganjil\n"
"- `slices[4]`: yang mempunyai gate `Ryy` bertindak pada semua pasangan qubit genap\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the cell below, we manually construct 4 `LayerError` instances for each one of these layers with some randomized error rates.\n"
msgstr "Dalam sel di bawah, kami membina secara manual 4 contoh `LayerError` untuk setiap satu lapisan ini dengan beberapa kadar ralat rawak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you would have used the `NoiseLearner` to identify the unique 2-qubit gate layers of your circuit and characterize their noise, you would obtain a `NoiseLearnerResult` object.\n"
"This result would contain a list of `LayerError` objects, just like the ones we have manually constructed above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda telah menggunakan `NoiseLearner` untuk mengenal pasti lapisan gate 2 qubit yang unik dalam litar anda dan mencirikan hingarnya, anda akan memperoleh objek `NoiseLearnerResult`.\n"
"Hasil ini akan mengandungi senarai objek `LayerError`, sama seperti yang telah kami bina secara manual di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each unique 2-qubit layer, the `LayerError` contains:\n"
"- the `QuantumCircuit` representing that 2-qubit gate layer\n"
"- the qubit indices which this circuit is acting upon\n"
"- the `PauliLindbladError` which represents the characterized noise model of this layer\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi setiap lapisan 2 qubit yang unik, `LayerError` mengandungi:\n"
"- `QuantumCircuit` yang mewakili lapisan gate 2 qubit tersebut\n"
"- indeks qubit yang menjadi sasaran litar ini\n"
"- `PauliLindbladError` yang mewakili model hingar tercirikan bagi lapisan ini\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `PauliLindbladError` will contain two objects:\n"
"- the list of Pauli errors that have been characterized\n"
"- the error rates corresponding to each one of those Pauli errors\n"
msgstr ""
"`PauliLindbladError` akan mengandungi dua objek:\n"
"- senarai ralat Pauli yang telah dicirikan\n"
"- kadar ralat yang sepadan dengan setiap satu ralat Pauli tersebut\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normally, the list of Pauli errors will be sparse. More specifically, it will contain the single-qubit Pauli errors on all qubits that have gates acting upon them as well as the two-qubit Pauli errors on all those qubits that are connected.\n"
msgstr "Lazimnya, senarai ralat Pauli akan jarang. Lebih khusus lagi, ia akan mengandungi ralat Pauli satu qubit pada semua qubit yang mempunyai gate bertindak ke atasnya serta ralat Pauli dua qubit pada semua qubit yang bersambung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inserting the noisy layers into our circuit {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"
msgstr "Memasukkan lapisan berhingar ke dalam litar kita {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we have specifically constructed one `LayerError` for each of our known unique 2-qubit gate layers.\n"
"This means, we know which `LayerError` matches a specific one of our slices exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bahagian sebelumnya, kita telah membina secara khusus satu `LayerError` bagi setiap lapisan gate 2 qubit unik yang kita ketahui.\n"
"Ini bermakna kita tahu `LayerError` mana yang sepadan tepat dengan satu hirisan tertentu kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, when using the `LayerError`, you will need to figure out what the unique 2-qubit gate layer is, and where it occurs inside of your circuit.\n"
"You will then need to adjust your `circuit` and/or `slices` to insert the `LayerError` accordingly.\n"
"How to do this in the general case, is beyond the scope of this how-to guide.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Here, our life is simpler because we know which slice a `LayerError` corresponds to.\n"
"Therefore, it is now just a matter of inserting new slices to represent the noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lazimnya, apabila menggunakan `LayerError`, anda perlu mengetahui apakah lapisan gate 2 qubit yang unik itu, dan di mana ia berlaku dalam litar anda.\n"
"Anda kemudian perlu melaraskan `circuit` dan/atau `slices` anda untuk memasukkan `LayerError` dengan sewajarnya.\n"
"Cara melakukannya dalam kes am adalah di luar skop panduan cara ini.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Di sini, keadaan kita lebih mudah kerana kita tahu hirisan mana yang sepadan dengan sesuatu `LayerError`.\n"
"Oleh itu, kini ia hanya soal memasukkan hirisan baharu untuk mewakili hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note, that we must wrap each `PauliLindbladError` from `LayerError.error` in a `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` for it to be a valid `QuantumCircuit` instruction.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa kita mesti membungkus setiap `PauliLindbladError` daripada `LayerError.error` dalam `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` supaya ia menjadi arahan `QuantumCircuit` yang sah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can check our work and draw the circuit below:\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menyemak kerja kita dan melukis litar di bawah:\n"

